# POSMena POS — General Rules

## Project Overview
Flutter kiosk/handheld POS for Saudi Arabia. Android only. Riverpod for new state. SQLite for local data. Dio for API.

## Architecture Quick Reference

| Layer | Location | Responsibility |
|-------|----------|----------------|
| Core | `lib/core/` | Config, helpers, routing, services, theme |
| Models | `lib/data/models/` | Pure data classes (no Flutter imports) |
| Local DB | `lib/data/services/local_data/` | SQLite tables |
| Remote API | `lib/data/services/remote_data/` | Dio-based API (interfaces + implementations) |
| Repository | `lib/repository/` | Business logic combining local + remote |
| Providers | `lib/providers/` | Riverpod StateNotifiers |
| Features | `lib/features/{kiosk,mobile,shared}-features/` | UI by mode |

## Critical Rules
- Use `dPrint()` not `print()` — see `lib/core/helpers/helper_functions.dart`
- Return `Either<Failure, T>` from data/repository methods — never throw across layers
- Route product taps through `ProductTapHandler.handleProductTap()` only
- Use `AppModeSession` for post-action route decisions — never hardcode mode checks in screens
- Use Riverpod for all new state management
- Each screen: `static const routePath` + `static const routeName`
- Navigate: `context.goNamed(WidgetName.routeName)`
- API services: call `await service.initialize()` before use
